<title>LEBANON: Slight decline in Lebanese treasury bill yields.</title>
<headline>Slight decline in Lebanese treasury bill yields.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Longer-term yields fell slightly on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its October 17 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		    Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  14.10 (14.10)	     14.61  (14.61)</p>
<p>    Six months	    15.60 (15.60)	     16.92  (16.92)</p>
<p>    12 months	     15.10 (15.11)	     17.78  (17.79)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 21.62  (21.64)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
</text>
